## Dependencies and services

Packages installed from `requirements.txt` retain their own licenses. They are
dependencies, not relicensed by this repository. In particular, text cleaning
loads `frequency_dictionary_en_82_765.txt` from the pinned `symspellpy` 6.7.7
package rather than redistributing a dictionary in this repository. The
[`symspellpy` code declares the MIT
License](https://github.com/mammothb/symspellpy/blob/v6.7.7/LICENSE), while
[SymSpell documents the dictionary](https://github.com/wolfgarbe/SymSpell#frequency-dictionary)
as an intersection of Google Books Ngram data ([CC BY
3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)) and SCOWL ([source
terms](https://wordlist.aspell.net/scowl-readme/)). Those source terms remain
applicable; this repository does not relicense the installed dictionary.
Geoapify requests and responses are governed by the user's agreement with
Geoapify; no response payload is bundled here.
